# dfki-quad Repository Overview

ROS 2 (Humble) quadruped locomotion stack for **Unitree Go2** and the **DFKI ULab** robot. Combines MPC, WBC, gait sequencing, Drake simulation, and Invariant EKF state estimation. All runs inside Docker.

## Workspace Layout

```
dfki-quad/
├── run_docker.sh, build_new_image.sh, new_docker_shell.sh  # Docker lifecycle
├── docker/Dockerfile                                        # Container image
└── ws/src/
    ├── interfaces/       # Custom ROS msgs/srvs — shared contract for all packages
    ├── common/           # Robot models (Pinocchio/Drake), URDF, shared params
    ├── controllers/      # MIT controller: gait sequencer → MPC → WBC
    ├── drivers/          # leg_driver (IK+safety), motor drivers (Unitree/mjbots)
    ├── simulator/        # Drake physics sim + Meshcat visualizer
    ├── state_estimation/ # Invariant EKF (used on real hardware)
    └── solver_experiments/ # ICRA25 QP solver benchmarking scripts
```

## Key Interfaces (ws/src/interfaces/)

All cross-package communication goes through custom types: `QuadState`, `QuadControlTarget`, `LegCmd`, `JointCmd`, `GaitSequence`, `WBCTarget`, `MPCDiagnostics`, `ResetSimulation`.

## Robot Selection

Robot is selected at **build time**: `-DROBOT_NAME=go2` or `-DROBOT_NAME=ulab`.
At **launch time**: `sim:=go2`, `sim:=ulab`, `real:=go2`, or `real:=ulab`.

## Research Tags

- `ICRA25` — QP solver comparison experiments
- `IROS25` — Online model adaptation (Kalman filter)
